<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<!--
  The human fallback behind Codify.

  This queue does double duty, deliberately. It is the fallback the routing flow
  hands work to when the agent cannot take it, and it is the owner group for the
  follow-up work Codify_EscalateForReviewInvocable raises when a recap is too
  thin to classify. Those are the same people in practice.

  Two properties are load-bearing for Omni-Channel routing, and routeWork fails
  outright without either:

  * queueRoutingConfig — a queue with no routing configuration is just a group of
    users. Without it routeWork reports "The referenced fallback queue must be an
    Omni-Channel queue" and the whole routing flow errors, so nothing reaches the
    agent at all.
  * queueSobject MessagingSession — the Messaging service channel routes
    MessagingSession records, not Cases. A queue that only supports Case cannot
    accept the work being routed.
-->
<Queue xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <doesSendEmailToMembers>false</doesSendEmailToMembers>
    <name>Codify Support Ops</name>
    <queueRoutingConfig>Codify_Routing_Configuration</queueRoutingConfig>
    <queueSobject>
        <sobjectType>MessagingSession</sobjectType>
    </queueSobject>
    <queueSobject>
        <sobjectType>Case</sobjectType>
    </queueSobject>
</Queue>
